{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfbT4rNjPiRk8jn5K5Lhd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Field and accessors on `Owner`** — the `deleted` column, getter/setter, and the `isDeleted()` null-tolerant helper live on the entity, which is the right unit. `isDeleted()` centralizes the \"null means not deleted\" rule so callers don't repeat `Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)`.\n- **Mapper helper** — `formatDeleted` follows the exact convention of the sibling `format*` helpers (null-owner guard, `default` method, `@Mapping(... expression)` wiring). It reads naturally alongside `formatTelephoneDisplay` etc.\n- **Service change** — `deleteOwner` swapping `delete` for `setDeleted(true)` + `save` is the minimal, correct place for the soft-delete behavior; it stays in the service layer where the other mutation logic lives.\n- **Duplicate/identity filters** — the added `.filter(existing -> !existing.isDeleted())` sits right next to the pre-existing `.filter(... getId ...)` in each of the three pipelines, mirroring the established per-check structure. Those three pipelines already each carry their own `findAll().stream().filter(...)`, so adding a parallel exclusion filter is the locally-consistent choice rather than a new catch-all; extracting a shared helper would be a broader refactor not invited by this spec.\n- **Schema + OpenAPI** — the column is added uniformly across all four DB dialects and the DTO is documented as `readOnly`, matching how the other derived fields are described.\n\nNothing is duplicated beyond what the surrounding code already establishes, and no class or method is turning into a catch-all."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9356,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens